    "result_text": "All tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI introduced address normalization applied whenever an owner is created, following the repository's established normalizer pattern.\n\n**New component** \u2014 `rest/validation/AddressNormalizer.java`:\n- Trims and collapses internal whitespace to single spaces\n- Upper-cases the text\n- Expands whole-word abbreviations (`ST`\u2192`STREET`, `RD`\u2192`ROAD`, `AVE`\u2192`AVENUE`) via a token-wise map lookup (so `MAIN`/`STREET` are untouched)\n- Returns `null` for `null` input and `\"\"` for input that is blank after trimming\n\nIt mirrors the single-responsibility, `@Component`, javadoc style of the sibling `EmailNormalizer`/`TelephoneNormalizer`.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`:\n- Injected `AddressNormalizer` via the constructor.\n- Normalize the DTO's `address` at the very start of `addOwner`, *before* the required-field check. This makes the normalized form the single source of truth for everything downstream:\n  - The existing `OwnerFieldsValidator` now rejects an address blank after normalization (`\"   \"` \u2192 `\"\"` \u2192 `isBlank()` \u2192 400), with no change to the validator itself.\n  - The mapper produces an `Owner` carrying the normalized address, so `applyHouseholdPolicy` (duplicate detection via `HouseholdKey`) and `HouseholdIdGenerator` both compare on the normalized form automatically.\n  - The stored and returned `address` is the normalized value.\n\nNo logic was duplicated \u2014 normalization lives in one place, and the household/validation code consumes the already-normalized entity. The full test suite (including the 3 new acceptance tests) is green.",
